# IBM's NCR driver (DD_SCSI0/DD_SCSI1 are the same 53C810 driver), in
# ncr_chip_reset_bus.  After pulsing SCSI RST/ it reads SIST0 once and then
# loops, up to 100,000 times with calibrated delays, re-reading ISTAT,
# SIST0, SIST1 and DSTAT until any of them shows something.  On the Network
# Server's 53C825A, ISTAT's SIP drops as soon as SIST0 is read (NT's
# miniport depends on that), so nothing ever shows.  The boot then sits in
# that loop for tens of billions of emulated instructions.  Run the loop
# body once: the back-branch at ncr_chip_reset_bus+0x4ec
# (bt lt, ncr_chip_reset_bus+0x288) becomes a nop.  Little-endian
# instruction bytes.
file /MK/DD_SCSI0.DYN
patch-sym ncr_chip_reset_bus+0x4ec 9cfd8041 00000060
file /MK/DD_SCSI1.DYN
patch-sym ncr_chip_reset_bus+0x4ec 9cfd8041 00000060
